{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And as for you, lift up your staff and stretch out your hand.</b> This verse should not be understood to mean that Moses lifted his staff over the sea, for it says only ״ויט משה את ידו״ — 'and Moses stretched out his hand.' Rather, the sense of הרם את מטך is 'remove it from your hand,' because there were among the people those lacking faith in Israel who said that Moses had no power to split the sea except by the power of the staff in his hand. Therefore He said, הרם את מטך — remove it from your hand. And so you find in the Midrash: they said, 'Moses has no power to do anything except by the staff — with it he struck the Nile, with it he brought all the plagues.' And when they came to the Sea of Reeds and Israel was standing there, the Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: 'Lift up your staff' — so that they should not say, 'Were it not for the staff, he could not have split the sea.' And therefore Scripture needed to say ״ואמינו בה׳ ובמשה עבדו״ — 'and they believed in HaShem and in Moses His servant.' What need is there to say ויאמינו, seeing that it was already stated ״ויאמן העם״? But because they reverted and did not believe, Scripture needed to state that now, at the splitting of the Sea of Reeds, they believed."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:58:59.564816407Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}